```
Reason:
The outer condition allows entry when `res_pool->ref_clocks.dchub_ref_clock_inKhz / 1000 != current_dchub_ref_freq` is true, even if `dc->res_pool->funcs->update_bw_bounding_box` is NULL. The inner check only verifies `dc->clk_mgr`, not the callback pointer, leading to a NULL pointer dereference when `update_bw_bounding_box` is called.

The code statements that fix the bug are:
```
dchub_ref_freq_changed =
    res_pool->ref_clocks.dchub_ref_clock_inKhz / 1000 != current_dchub_ref_freq;
if ((!dc->debug.fams2_config.bits.enable || dchub_ref_freq_changed) &&
    dc->res_pool->funcs->update_bw_bounding_box &&
    dc->clk_mgr && dc->clk_mgr->bw_params) {
    dc->res_pool->funcs->update_bw_bounding_box(dc, dc->clk_mgr->bw_params);
}
```
Reason:
The fix separates the frequency change check into a boolean variable and adds explicit null checks for `dc->res_pool->funcs->update_bw_bounding_box`, `dc->clk_mgr`, and `dc->clk_mgr->bw_params` before calling the function. This ensures that the callback is only invoked when all required pointers are valid, preventing the NULL pointer dereference.

